## Why This Is Asked

Tests for data-import flows are common in cloud applications. This question evaluates practical E2E thinking at a beginner level, covering end-to-end flow, UI feedback, and data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end flow of uploading data and handling background processing
- Mocking backend services (job queue) for deterministic, reliable tests
- Data seeding to ensure predictable idempotent behavior
- Verifying UI progress indicators and downloadable summary reports

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright snippet illustrating route mocking and upload
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('data import workflow with progress and idempotency', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed database with existing records for idempotency testing
  await seedTestData();

  // Mock the job queue response
  await page.route('**/api/import', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      body: JSON.stringify({ jobId: 'test-job-123', status: 'processing' })
    });
  });

  // Upload CSV fixture
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');

  // Verify live progress updates
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-bar')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-text')).toContainText('100%');

  // Verify invalid rows are highlighted
  await expect(page.locator('.invalid-row')).toHaveCount(5);

  // Download and verify summary report
  const [download] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('.download-summary')
  ]);

  const report = await download.text();
  expect(report).toContain('Total: 500');
  expect(report).toContain('Valid: 495');
  expect(report).toContain('Invalid: 5');

  // Test idempotency - re-upload same file
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');
  await page.waitForSelector('.upload-complete');

  // Verify no duplicates were created
  const recordCount = await getRecordCount();
  expect(recordCount).toBe(500);
});
```

